    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107645" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέρκομπος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>overweening, arrogant,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ὑ. θηρῶσα Φάων᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					312
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς ὑπερκόμποις σαγαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					391
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῆμ᾽ ὑπέρκομπον τόδε</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				404
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ὑπερκόμπων ἄγαν φρονημάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					827
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερκόμπῳ θράσει</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				831
			</span></i>: c. dat. modi, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ δ᾽ ὑπέρκομποι
				τάχει [νῆες</span>] <i>extraordinary,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				342
			</span></i> (s. v. l.). Cf. sq.</div>
